{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Pins | The Faith Received</title>
<meta name="description" content="Your collections. Now part of the Notebook tab of the Research desk." />
{{!-- Someone's own reading notes were never in an index and this
      forwarding page should not be either. --}}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://mereorthodoxy.com/the-faith-received/research/" />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /the-faith-received/pins/ — a redirect into the Research desk.

     WHAT HAPPENED, AND IT IS NOT THE SAME AS COMPARE AND THE DESK.
     Those two became tabs. Pins did not: it became the collection strip
     INSIDE the Notebook tab, because it had never been a second place
     to keep anything. A collection has only ever held entry ids into
     the notebook (see assets/js/lib/faith-collections-store.js), and
     the tell was that a passage kept while reading turned up on the
     Pins page under "Not in a collection" without the reader having
     filed it. That is the behaviour of a filter, not of a destination.
     The reasoning is set out in full at the top of
     partials/faith-received/_notebook-panel.hbs.

     NOTHING WAS LOST IN THE MOVE. Named collections with their counts,
     the working notes on each one, cards in the reader's own order, the
     relations drawn between two passages with their ring and their
     list, and the Markdown copy, download and share are all in that
     panel. The one thing that did not survive is the page's own card
     renderer, which duplicated the notebook entry beside it with a
     weaker note field.

     WHY THIS URL STILL EXISTS. Pins carried no state in its address, so
     unlike Compare there is no view to rebuild. It exists so that a
     bookmark to it lands on the reader's collections instead of on a
     404, and so that the copy on the way through says where they went.
     If Ian would rather this one 404'd, this is the template to delete
     and the routes.yaml entry to drop; the other two are not.

     THE TRANSFORM. Straight to the Notebook tab, which is where the
     collections are:

       /the-faith-received/pins/  -> /research/#notebook

     location.replace, not assign, so Back from the Research desk does
     not bounce through here.

     WITHOUT SCRIPT there is a real link, and it is the whole content of
     the page rather than a hidden fallback. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">
  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a></p>
      <h1>Pins has moved</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">Your collections now live in the Notebook tab of the Research desk, beside the passages they gather. Nothing has changed about what is in them.</p>
      <p class="bhero-sub"><a href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook">Open your notebook and collections</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<script>
  (function () {
    // Nothing to carry: Pins kept no state in its address.
    window.location.replace("/the-faith-received/research/#notebook");
  })();
</script>
